From cdd6a1ca8eed617d3c4f0fe6e1918216694d5cf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:44:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] arrange: count the pretest's kills in the -DPROFILE
 counters

The pretest returns from TRY_CHILD before the PROFILE block at its end,
so in a -DPROFILE build the children it kills were missing from
prof_created / prof_kids / prof_pruned, and the per-depth profile
changed with --pretest-min. Count them there as created and pruned; the
counters now agree with the pretest on and off (bench/quick.txt S=517
and S=648, every depth).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
---
 src/c/arrange_core.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/c/arrange_core.h b/src/c/arrange_core.h
index 113ea9b..65c9923 100644
--- a/src/c/arrange_core.h
+++ b/src/c/arrange_core.h
@@ -1189,6 +1189,12 @@ static inline TRY_CHILD_INLINE void TRY_CHILD(sstate_t *s, int d, int b,
       }
       cp_die[pl][why]++;
       cp_pt_kill[pl]++;
+#endif
+#ifdef PROFILE
+      /* (as at the end of TRY_CHILD: a child created and pruned) */
+      prof_created[d + 1]++;
+      prof_kids[d]++;
+      prof_pruned[d + 1]++;
 #endif
       s->np[b]--;
       return;
-- 
